<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Fast tests for the Tenancy platform module (docs/architecture/testing-strategy.md 2): the
    registry's value objects and entity invariants, the EF value converter, the model-to-snapshot
    check, the ADR-0007 9.3 guard over the catalog *model*, and (Kernel/, B-06.1a) the tenancy
    kernel types of Aurora.Platform.Tenancy.Contracts - TenantAccess, TenantScope, SchemaVersion
    and the rest - including the construction tests that prove ADR-0007 3.4's "no module can
    fabricate a TenantScope" link by link.

    This is the one test assembly the contracts project grants InternalsVisibleTo, which is what
    lets the kernel tests call TenantScope's internal constructor; the grant list is asserted as an
    exact set in TenantAccessConstructionTests.

    Nothing here opens a connection. Building an EF model needs the Npgsql provider's type
    mappings but no database, so these run in verify.sh stage 6 with Docker stopped. The guard's
    twin over the *migrated schema* lives in the integration project.

    FsCheck carries the ordering law of SchemaVersion over arbitrary ordinals, from a plain [Fact]
    via QuickCheckThrowOnFailure, as Aurora.SharedKernel.UnitTests already does.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Aurora.Platform.Tenancy.UnitTests</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" />
    <PackageReference Include="Shouldly" />
    <PackageReference Include="FsCheck" />
    <PackageReference Include="coverlet.collector" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\src\platform\Aurora.Platform.Tenancy\Aurora.Platform.Tenancy.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
